# Scratch directories from structural repair passes. Each file is a point-in-time
# copy of a canonical document taken before a renumbering or insertion step, kept
# only so an in-progress operation is recoverable on the working machine.
# Provenance lives in git history, so these must not enter it.
.renumber-backup/

# Python bytecode from running the verifier and its mutation battery.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# pytest cache. The battery at tools/test_verify_contract_graph.py is standalone
# and pytest collects no tests from it, but an exploratory `pytest` invocation
# still writes this directory. Caches hold no provenance; git history does.
.pytest_cache/

# Rust (NirmanSupervisor.exe) build outputs.
/target/
**/target/

# C#/.NET WinUI 3 (Nirman.exe) build, restore, and IDE outputs.
**/bin/
**/obj/
*.user
.vs/

# Local runtime state, SQLite state files, and generated task artifacts.
.runtime/
.task-data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# AI assistant work trees and configuration directories.
.workbuddy/
.workbuddy-ai/
.kilo/
.kilocode/
.freebuff/
.kombai/
scratch/

# Credential stores and other secret material that a local agent host may write inside the
# working tree (git credential helpers, provider tokens, signing keystores). The agent
# environment keeps its token at ~/.secrets/github-git-credentials, outside this repository,
# and no remote URL in .git/config embeds a credential; this entry is the backstop that keeps
# a stray copy from ever being staged onto main. Secrets never belong in provenance.
#
# Patterns are anchored to secret-shaped FILES, never to bare substrings. An unanchored
# `*token*` / `*credentials*` also matches legitimate source — `crates/nirman-ipc/src/token.rs`,
# `credentials_broker.rs`, and (under Windows' default core.ignorecase) `CancellationTokenSource.cs`
# — which would be dropped from the tree silently. Keep these anchored.
.secrets/
*.token
*.credentials
*.credentials.json
# Anchored to a filename suffix, per the rule above. The unanchored forms this
# replaces also swallowed `fixtures/design-tokens.json` and `fixtures/figma/
# tokens.json`, which the design-token import path legitimately produces.
# `*token.json` still catches `token.json` and `github-token.json`;
# `*credentials.json` still catches `provider-credentials.json`.
*token.json
*credentials.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks
